# Runtime data directories. In production these are named volumes
# (uploads_data, staging_data) mounted over the image's own empty dirs, so a
# host copy is never read — but `COPY . .` would still tar every byte into the
# build context first. A dev staging/ of a few gigabytes turns a fast build
# into a slow one for nothing.
staging/
uploads/

# Secrets never belong in a build context.
.env
.env.*

# Local database dumps.
backups/

.git/
